      "body": "> Maybe stick with a single option 'sp_info' or something, which would be the list of sp addresses of each output, or an empty list for regular transactions?\n\nI'm not sure this is enough to make users actively think about SP payments unless you are suggesting that the `sp_info` parameter be required?\n\n> and it feels less aggressive than forcing 99% of the use cases to set force=true everytime?\n\nWhere does the 99% figure come from? I’d expect most users not to have the same keys loaded in multiple wallets. The main exception is setups that pair an offline signer with an online watch-only wallet.",
