      "body": "> 3\\. I'm not sure this is enough to make users actively think about SP payments unless you are suggesting that the `sp_info` parameter be required?\n\nYes, i was thinking about making this one mandatory, which seems clearer than having a 'force' argument that has to be here for all non-silent payment txs without having a name giving context what it is for\n\n> 3\\. Where does the 99% figure come from? I’d expect most users not to have the same keys loaded in multiple wallets. The main exception is setups that pair an offline signer with an online watch-only wallet.\n\nThat was my rough idea that ~1% of bumpfee calls would be for silent payments once the feature is merged.\nActually, I think it would be the main pain point of integrating this: forcing almost everyone to add an argument they don't use, just because the node can't know if an external transaction contains silent payments?\n\nAlso, I was actually expecting the bumpfee could only be used for silent payments if the tx is paid by a wallet known by the node receiving the rpc request? But maybe the SP instructions can transmit the new S value or something like that without making the sender's private keys computable by another node?\n\nI might not have fully understood the request yet, but I would be interested in working on it\n",
